\begin{abstract}
The Temporal Symmetry Systems Engine (TSSE) is a unified Hamiltonian, symplectic,
and temporal-invariant architecture designed for high-performance relativistic
propulsion systems, including the Antimatter-Initiated Thermonuclear Fusion Engine
(AITFE). This article presents the journal-form condensation of the TSSE monograph,
